    "body": "Exploring a hypothetical scenario for local LLM inference, this post considers the relationship between batch size and aggregate throughput. It's important to preface this by stating that these are purely illustrative figures, not measured results from any actual experiment. The hypothetical data suggests that a batch size of 1 yielded an aggregate throughput of 22 tokens per second. In contrast, increasing the batch size to 4 hypothetically resulted in an aggregate throughput of 55 tokens per second.\n\nThese values represent overall system throughput, not per-request performance, and per-request latency was not evaluated. The intention is to initiate a technical discussion on how batching strategies might impact overall processing capacity in local LLM setups, emphasizing the synthetic and illustrative nature of these numbers.",
